commit d9cbed0c61929353e17b77b90cacd67e7c192a69
Author:     Jakub Skokan <jakub.skokan@havefun.cz>
AuthorDate: Wed Oct 7 16:15:40 2026 +0200
Commit:     Jakub Skokan <jakub.skokan@havefun.cz>
CommitDate: Fri Oct 9 23:24:18 2026 +0200

    runtime: add portable KB launcher and capture leases
    
    Use one standalone engine for checkout and packaged cluster commands. Private
    versioned identities, prepared artifacts and fresh run receipts bind owned
    resources to immutable source and full-lifetime capture leases. Cold resume
    retains the accepted artifact; updates prepare exact guest closures before
    stopping and preserve owned disks and credentials. Require unchanged resolved
    SSH endpoints so retained host-key trust remains valid after the restart.
    Public lifecycle contention refuses before mutation rather than queuing it.
    
    Capture and validation share explicit connection and artifact-root contracts,
    with canonical source proof and bilingual result preservation. Keep the
    artifact flock in the writing process through publication and cleanup so a
    helper failure cannot admit a competing writer during synchronous writes.
    Observed lease loss cancels capture and prevents subsequent publication.
    
    Verify the installed tools directly on an ordinary Linux/Nix/KVM host through
    public commands, with exact predecessor continuity and measured capacity. The
    selected IP inventory fixture uses a small member VPS and dedicated
    administrator API provisioning while retaining a proved member browser. Expose
    a separate strict hosted check for the accepted committed media.
    
    Discover all machine SSH keys within one readiness deadline, retaining private
    native diagnostics and refusing partial or changed trust. Preserve child PID
    authority atomically across supported interruption and close owned resources.
    Give the runner its own POSIX session before machine creation; containing
    cgroup and host failures still require complete ownership and exit proof.
    Quiesce its control thread before closing the listener, and preserve primary
    fixture failures and native private diagnostics without accepting unknown
    socket contents.
    
    Pin the private directory and socket inode during authenticated live shutdown.
    The same locked stop or update may retire only that unchanged control socket
    after acknowledged shutdown and complete exit proof for the same launch and
    runner. The verifier uses final-controller stop, genuine predecessor resume
    and final-controller update. Interruption discards this permission; a dead
    residual cannot reconstruct it from saved path or inode facts.
    
    Use the configured machine budget for one graceful shutdown and keep the
    original runner, tracker, listener and reapers alive until owned children
    exit. Require the exact run-ready marker for status, connection and capture so
    slow shutdown never retains capture readiness. Caller timeout keeps the same
    run and does not grant force or restart authority.
    Notify the first accepted stop even if acknowledgement delivery fails, so
    caller loss cannot strand a latched run before its graceful drain.
    
    Read child lists from every task of each reached process. Retain observed
    identities across reparenting and treat observed task changes as inconclusive.
    Quiesce tracking and prove exit before explicit machine cleanup, then collect
    fresh proof before completion. Sequential procfs reads do not establish an
    atomic process-tree snapshot or recover missing historical ownership.
    
    Legacy state and sockets remain untouched rather than being adopted by the new
    engine.

commit 922e71e5eb75b6eb416bf55e39160e9a7236e654
Author:     Jakub Skokan <jakub.skokan@havefun.cz>
